.TH CIRCULAR_QUEUE_CREATE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
circular_queue_create \- create a circular queue
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadcomm.h>

circular_queue_create(max_size, err_str);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Creates a fixed-size bounded queue that uses a circular buffer internally.
Send operations block when the queue is full until space becomes available.
Uses standard malloc/free for memory management.

This is a convenience macro for circular_queue_create_with_mprocs() with
NULL memory management procedures.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
max_size  Maximum number of messages the queue can hold (1 to
          SIZE_MAX / sizeof(c_message_t); a larger value is rejected,
          since the queue is backed by a single max_size * sizeof(c_message_t)
          array and a larger value would overflow that computation)
err_str   Optional pointer to receive error string on failure
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns pointer to newly created circular queue on success
Returns NULL on failure
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
All operations on this queue are thread-safe
Queue must be destroyed with circular_queue_destroy() when done
fork(2) is safe with respect to this queue's own internal locking: a
lock held by some other thread at the instant of the fork is never
inherited by the child already locked. The queue owns no thread of
its own, so one already live and in active use across the fork
remains fully usable on both sides afterward.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR circular_queue_create_with_mprocs (3),
.BR circular_queue_destroy (3)
